# ─── Instance ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=4000
HOST=0.0.0.0
# Comma-separate multiple origins. Any subdomain of SITE_BASE_DOMAIN is allowed (credentialed unless it is a school's own site).
CORS_ORIGIN=https://akoro.name.ng,https://app.akoro.name.ng,https://instructors.akoro.name.ng

# ─── Platform addresses (lib/urls.js is the only place these defaults live) ───
# Each falls back to the CURRENT host shown here when unset, but production should set them: a fallback is silent in the
# product, and the API logs a warning at boot naming any that are missing.
FRONTEND_URL=https://app.akoro.name.ng                 # the learner app: emails, sign-in links, payment returns
MAIN_SITE_URL=https://akoro.name.ng                    # the marketing site: legal links, school-site "home"
INSTRUCTOR_FRONTEND_URL=https://instructors.akoro.name.ng
ADMIN_FRONTEND_URL=https://admin.akoro.name.ng
SCHOOL_FRONTEND_URL=https://akoro-school.akoro.name.ng # the school portal
# AGENT_FRONTEND_URL=https://agent.akoro.name.ng
# BUSINESS_FRONTEND_URL=https://business.akoro.name.ng
API_URL=https://api.akoro.name.ng                      # this API as seen from outside (OAuth callbacks)
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=https://api.akoro.name.ng/api/auth/google/callback   # must match the Google console exactly
# Wildcard base domain for school sites (<slug>.SITE_BASE_DOMAIN). Set it EXPLICITLY — never derive it from FRONTEND_URL.
SITE_BASE_DOMAIN=akoro.name.ng
# EMAIL_ASSET_BASE=                                    # where email images are served (default FRONTEND_URL)
# JWT_ISSUER / JWT_AUDIENCE are opaque claims inside issued tokens, NOT addresses. Leave them as they are in production —
# changing them signs every user out.
SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=30000

# ─── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=your-service-role-key
# (Some legacy agent modules read SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — an alias for the
#  same service-role secret. They fall back to SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY, so one
#  var is enough; set the alias only if you prefer.)
# Per-instance Postgres pool size for the runtime pool (adaptive chat).
# Keep it SURPRISINGLY SMALL: Supavisor, the external proxy in front of
# Supabase Postgres, absorbs traffic spikes — a big pool just parks idle
# connections in Postgres where they cost RAM and context switches.
# Budget: DB_POOL_MAX × instances + 1 migration client ≤ project limit.
DB_POOL_MAX=5
DB_POOL_IDLE_MS=10000                # close idle server connections after 10s
DB_POOL_CONNECT_MS=5000              # fail fast when the pool is exhausted
DB_READ_URL=                         # optional read replica
# General Postgres URI (NOT the Supabase REST URL). Point this at the Supavisor
# TRANSACTION POOLER — Supabase: Connect → Connection string → Transaction
# pooler, i.e. aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543 with user
# postgres.<project-ref>. The runtime pool only issues stateless
# pool.query() calls (no session state, no named prepared statements), so
# transaction pooling is safe. Do NOT use the direct db.<ref>.supabase.co
# host here — its connection budget is small and shared with PostgREST.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.your-project-ref:password@aws-0-your-region.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# Optional migration-only override. The migration runner prefers this URL and
# runs DDL, which wants a session/direct connection (db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432
# or the pooler's session port 5432) rather than the transaction pooler.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@db.your-project.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# ─── Redis ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
REDIS_URL=redis://default:password@your-redis:6379

# ─── Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
JWT_SECRET=change-this-to-a-long-random-string
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d
BCRYPT_ROUNDS=10

# ─── Internal secret (worker callback) ───────────────────────
INTERNAL_SECRET=change-this-to-another-random-secret

# ─── Python agent private gateway ─────────────────────────────
# Matches AKORO_AGENT_TOOLS_SECRET in the Python service. This allows only the
# deployed Python service to call its tools and durable conversation-context
# routes under /api/internal/agent-tools/v1.
AKORO_AGENT_TOOLS_SECRET=change-this-to-a-third-long-random-secret
# Separate signing key for short-lived, session-bound toolContext capability
# tokens minted inside the authenticated Akoro API → Python bridge. Never send
# it to Python or a browser.
AKORO_AGENT_TOOLS_CAPABILITY_SECRET=change-this-to-a-fourth-long-random-secret
# Trusted Node → Python bridge used only after a learner confirms a staged
# write. The browser never receives this secret or the confirmation token.
# Direct Postgres connection string for the migration engine (Supabase →
# Project Settings → Database → Connection string URI). When set, the API
# applies pending schema migrations itself at every boot — no host release
# hook needed (MIGRATIONS_ON_BOOT=false to disable). Without it you must run
# `npm run db:migrate` by hand after each schema-changing deploy.
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgres://…:5432/postgres
# MIGRATIONS_ON_BOOT=true

PYTHON_AGENT_SERVICE_URL=https://your-agent-service.example
AKORO_AGENT_SERVICE_SECRET=change-this-to-a-fifth-long-random-secret
# Python's optional canonical teaching-workflow bridge uses the existing
# AKORO_AGENT_TOOLS_SECRET plus learner toolContext. Its live sessions are
# process-affine, so configure sticky routing or one API replica for the route.
AKORO_TEACHING_WORKFLOW_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=1800
# Durable Agent Chat context on POST /api/adaptive/chat/agent is ON by default
# in code (server-owned bounded exact history, compact summary, learner-clearable
# study memory, semantic retrieval, structured scratchpad). Set to "false" only
# to force the plain-transcript fallback on a lagging environment — the
# transcript itself still saves either way once the client sends a session.
AKORO_AGENT_CHAT_DURABLE_CONTEXT_ENABLED=true
# Feature-gated learner read tools on the unified Agent Chat endpoint.
# Concept Tracker and Learning Insights stay opt-in (off until their matching
# migration and learner controls are authorised and deployed); the exam-prep
# confidence loop, adaptive workflow projections and the study-prep session
# loop are DEFAULT-ON kill switches (the peer-consult pattern): absent env
# means enabled, =false removes the slice everywhere at once.
AKORO_CONCEPT_TRACKER_ENABLED=false
AKORO_LEARNER_INSIGHTS_ENABLED=false
AKORO_EXAM_PREP_CONFIDENCE_ENABLED=true
AKORO_ADAPTIVE_WORKFLOWS_ENABLED=true
# Study-prep session loop (agent + harness + education engine). Requires the
# 2026-study-prep-sessions-v1 migration. Plan-only in chat; the learner
# confirms spend on the plan card rendered in the Agent Chat tab.
AKORO_STUDY_PREP_ENABLED=true

# ─── Autonomy heartbeat cadence (background planner) ──────────
# THE LOOP — one variable, no overnight wait: while the agent is online
# the planner re-reviews on this pace, any time of day.
#   AKORO_AUTONOMY_CYCLE_EVERY=5m    test rig
#   AKORO_AUTONOMY_CYCLE_EVERY=1h    hourly reviews
# Units s/m/h/d (or raw ms), minimum 1m. Implies continuous mode (the
# nightly window is bypassed) and the scheduler tick derives itself.
# Budgets still apply per learner: the weekly run budget below (raise it
# or the loop pauses when it's spent) and the 5-pending-proposals inbox
# cap (an unattended inbox pauses proposing until the learner acts).
# All values apply at boot — change the env, restart, done; unset or
# invalid values keep the defaults.
AKORO_AUTONOMY_CYCLE_EVERY=               # empty = nightly (default)
# Fine-grained controls (CYCLE_EVERY usually replaces these):
AKORO_AUTONOMY_MODE=nightly               # nightly (default) | continuous
AKORO_AUTONOMY_TICK_MS=60000              # scheduler wake-up (min 5000)
AKORO_AUTONOMY_BATCH_LIMIT=40             # learners claimed per tick
AKORO_AUTONOMY_MIN_CYCLE_MS=              # per-learner pace in ms; empty = use hours below
AKORO_AUTONOMY_MIN_CYCLE_HOURS=20         # per-learner pace, whole hours
AKORO_AUTONOMY_WINDOW_START_HOUR=21       # nightly window start, hour 0-23
AKORO_AUTONOMY_WINDOW_END_HOUR=22         # end; start>end wraps midnight, start==end = planner off
AKORO_AUTONOMY_TRIGGER_COOLDOWN_MS=900000 # event-trigger cooldown per user+kind (min 1000)
AKORO_AUTONOMY_MAX_WEEKLY_RUNS=30         # weekly planner budget per learner (cycle.js enforces)

# ─── Background jobs ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Every recurring job (embedding sweep, alerts, evals, autonomy/follow-up
# workers, routine scheduler, tenant refresh) burns DB commands while the
# process runs. Set to false on metered/free deployments with no real traffic;
# the API stays fully functional, only periodic jobs stand down.
AKORO_BACKGROUND_JOBS_ENABLED=true

# ── Scheduled-job clock (cf/cron-ticker) ─────────────────────────────
# local (default): node-cron fires the nightly jobs inside this process.
# cloudflare: the edge Worker (cf/cron-ticker) fires them via
# POST /api/internal/ticks/:name — on-time across deploys, wakes a
# sleeping instance, UTC. Set this ONLY once the ticker is deployed,
# or nothing fires the nightly jobs.
# CRON_SOURCE=cloudflare

# ─── Redis quota forensics (local only) ─────────────────────
# Set true to log a stack trace + call-site for EVERY Redis command and a
# per-minute tally. Defaults off — zero behaviour change in production.
AKORO_REDIS_TRACE=false
# AKORO_REDIS_TRACE_MAX=300      per-command console lines before the tally-only mode

# ─── Video encoding worker ───────────────────────────────────
# The encoding worker (worker.js, separate service) polls BullMQ. Set to
# "false" on per-command-billed Redis (Upstash free) when you are not
# encoding videos — an idle worker with defaults burns tens of thousands of
# commands a day.
VIDEO_WORKER_ENABLED=true

# ─── Platform commission ──────────────────────────────────────
PLATFORM_COMMISSION_PERCENT=20
PAYOUT_MINIMUM_KOBO=500000

# ─── Cloudflare R2 ────────────────────────────────────────────
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-r2-access-key
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-r2-secret-key
R2_BUCKET_NAME=akoro-videos
R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://cdn.akoro.io

# Library record uploads work WITHOUT the R2_* variables: files up to 5 MB
# go to a private Supabase Storage bucket (created automatically on first
# upload). Larger files still need R2. The same bucket is the failure lane
# when R2 IS configured: R2 is primary, and while it's unreachable files
# up to 5 MB ride Supabase so a store outage doesn't stop small uploads.
# Optional bucket override:
# SUPABASE_RECORDS_BUCKET=akoro-records

# ─── Meeting platforms ────────────────────────────────────────
ZOOM_CLIENT_ID=
ZOOM_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDIRECT_URI_ZOOM=https://api.akoro.app/api/meeting/auth/callback/zoom
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDIRECT_URI_GOOGLE=https://api.akoro.app/api/meeting/auth/callback/google
TEAMS_CLIENT_ID=
TEAMS_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDIRECT_URI_TEAMS=https://api.akoro.app/api/meeting/auth/callback/teams
# YouTube Live — enable YouTube Data API v3 in Google Cloud Console
# Can reuse GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET if the same OAuth client has YouTube scopes,
# or create a separate OAuth client for cleaner scope isolation.
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDIRECT_URI_YOUTUBE=https://api.akoro.app/api/meeting/auth/callback/youtube

# ─── Email ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@akoro.app

# ─── Twilio SMS / WhatsApp ────────────────────────────────────
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=+1234567890
DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE=234

# ─── Web Push (VAPID) ─────────────────────────────────────────
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_EMAIL=admin@akoro.io

# ─── Voucher redemption (learner top-up / checkout by code) ───
# Akoro's OWN API key on the voucher platform — issued from the business app
# (Akoro Business → API Keys). Used server-side to redeem learner voucher
# codes. SECRET: never expose this to a frontend bundle; anyone holding it
# could redeem every outstanding voucher this startup has issued.
VOUCHER_API_KEY=sk_live_your_voucher_key
# Where the voucher module lives. Defaults to this same API (it's mounted
# here today) — point it at the standalone service if/when it's split out.
# VOUCHER_API_URL=https://vouchers.akoro.app

# ⚠️ Exchange rate used to convert USD wallet amounts to NGN for Paystack
# top-ups AND payouts. Defaults to 1600 if unset — an unset/stale value
# silently mis-prices real money. Set it explicitly and review it.
USD_NGN_RATE=1600

# Platform's cut of each redemption, in percent (default 10, clamped 0-50).
VOUCHER_PLATFORM_FEE_PCT=10

# Where an agent is sent back to after a Paystack wallet top-up.
VOUCHERS_FRONTEND_URL=https://akoro-agent.vercel.app

# Outbound webhooks to startups' own backends (redemption notifications).
# The delivery worker runs on every replica; rows are claimed with
# FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED so each delivery is sent exactly once.
# VOUCHER_WEBHOOKS=off              disable the delivery worker
# VOUCHER_WEBHOOK_BATCH=20          deliveries claimed per minute-tick
# VOUCHER_WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT_MS=8000   per-request timeout
# VOUCHER_WEBHOOK_STALE_MINS=10     requeue deliveries stuck mid-flight

# ─── Paystack ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_your_key
PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_live_your_key
# Full webhook URL (must match the one set in the Paystack dashboard). Only its
# PATH is read by code — the unified webhook router is mounted on that path.
# Paystack signs webhooks with PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY — there is no separate
# webhook secret.
PAYSTACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://api.akoro.name.ng/api/webhooks/paystack
# Legacy mixed-purpose app base (monolith era: app + API shared one origin).
# Its money-critical use is the Paystack verify callback for course bundles
# and gifts — ${APP_URL}/api/payments/verify is a BACKEND route — so it MUST
# be the API's public URL. Some older user-facing link builders (email login
# links, gift redeem) also read it and really want FRONTEND_URL; migrating
# them is a pending cleanup. Until then one value serves the payment flow.
APP_URL=https://api.akoro.name.ng

# ─── Worker / FFmpeg (VPS only) ──────────────────────────────
FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg
FFPROBE_PATH=ffprobe
TEMP_DIR=./temp
WORKER_CONCURRENCY=1
# THE backend API's own public URL (the primary self-referencing base). The
# standalone media worker (worker.js) calls the API at this base, and the
# admin billing setup page builds the Paystack webhook URL from it.
API_BASE_URL=https://api.akoro.name.ng

# ─── Adaptive Learning Module ─────────────────────────────────
# OpenAI — powers ALL AI: agent loops (tasks, battle, chat, instructor
# tools, agentService), GPT-4o agents, embeddings, Whisper STT, realtime
# transcription, and tts-1 speech (single key for all voice/AI).
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-key
# Model for the agent loops (task tools, battle gen, chat tools). Optional —
# defaults to gpt-4o-mini (the tutor-chat model).
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ── JWT RS256 (generate with: node -e "const {generateKeyPairSync}=require('crypto'); ...") ──
JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=     # RSA-2048 private key PEM (\n-escaped as single line)
JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=      # RSA-2048 public  key PEM (\n-escaped as single line)
JWT_ISSUER=https://api.akoro.app
JWT_AUDIENCE=https://akoro.app
FRONTEND_URL=https://akoro.app
INSTRUCTOR_FRONTEND_URL=https://instructor.akoro.app
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=https://api.akoro.app/api/auth/google/callback

# ── Multi-tenant school sites (custom domains via Vercel) ────────────
# Token + project id of the SCHOOL FRONTEND Vercel project. When set, adding
# a custom domain attaches it to the project (TXT verify + automatic SSL).
VERCEL_TOKEN=
VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=
VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
# Base domain for wildcard tenant subdomains (<slug>.akoro.app)
SITE_BASE_DOMAIN=akoro.app

# ── Marketing lead-scout (admin Marketing page) ──────────────────────
# Python service in /lead-scout — finds schools + audits their websites.
LEAD_SCOUT_URL=http://localhost:8100
LEAD_SCOUT_SECRET=
# Optional richer sources for lead-scout itself (set in ITS environment):
#   GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY / YELP_API_KEY

# ── Resilience: circuit breakers + load shedding (api-security-hardening) ──
# Breakers wrap every OpenAI call (chat, streams, embeddings). When the
# provider degrades, requests fail fast with 503 + Retry-After instead of each
# burning a full SDK timeout. State is visible in /health ("breakers").
BREAKER_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
BREAKER_ERROR_PCT=50
BREAKER_RESET_MS=30000
# Event-loop lag (ms) and RSS (MB) bars past which the API sheds non-essential
# traffic (503 + Retry-After). Auth + /health are never shed. On Render Hobby
# (~512MB) keep SHED_MEM_MB below the instance limit.
SHED_LAG_MS=500
SHED_MEM_MB=450
SHED_RETRY_AFTER_S=5

# ── Backpressure: max queue depth before enqueues are rejected (503) ──
# An honest "at capacity, retry" beats a job that runs an hour late.
QUEUE_MAX_TASKS=500
QUEUE_MAX_EVALS=500
QUEUE_MAX_FOLLOWUPS=500
QUEUE_MAX_AUTONOMY=500

# ── Per-school tenant quota (hardening plan §3.2) ─────────────────
# School-site traffic is attributed by Origin and limited per minute.
# Tiers match the Admin tier model; generous by design (a classroom
# bursting together is ~300 req/min). A school's api_quota_per_min
# column overrides its tier. TENANT_QUOTA=off disables enforcement.
TENANT_QUOTA=on
QUOTA_PILOT_PER_MIN=600
QUOTA_FREEMIUM_PER_MIN=1200
QUOTA_PREMIUM_PER_MIN=3000

# ── Proxy trust (client → Cloudflare → Render → Node) ────────────────────────
# Hop count in X-Forwarded-For that Express should trust when resolving req.ip.
# With Cloudflare proxying (orange cloud) in front of Render the chain is:
#   visitor, Cloudflare edge, Render ingress  →  TRUST_PROXY=2
# (without Cloudflare it was 1). If this is wrong, req.ip resolves to a PROXY
# address and every visitor behind it shares ONE app rate-limit bucket.
# app.js logs "[security] first request — req.ip=… x-forwarded-for=… trustProxy=…"
# on boot and warns with the number to use — set it to whatever that reports.
TRUST_PROXY=2

# ── Hugging Face mirror console (modules/hfmirror) ───────────────────────────
# Copies a HF model repo into your own account from the browser:
#   GET  /api/hf/mirror        — the console (key-guarded, like PHARMD_UPLOAD_KEY)
#   POST /api/hf/mirror        — start { source, target?, private?, dryRun? }
#   GET  /api/hf/mirror/status — job progress/log
# HF_MIRROR_KEY   — the console's shared secret (any long random string)
# HF_TOKEN        — a WRITE token for the DESTINATION account
#                   (hf.co/settings/tokens → "Write"). Also the default
#                   source token — for gated sources, the account that
#                   accepted the model's licence must own this token.
# HF_SOURCE_TOKEN — optional separate READ token for the source account.
# HF_MAX_FILE_MB  — per-file size cap (default 8192). Files over the cap
#                   are skipped and reported — Render disks are small.
# HF_MIRROR_KEY=change-me-long-random-string
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# HF_SOURCE_TOKEN=hf_yyy
# HF_MAX_FILE_MB=8192

# ── Record text extraction (hanji-parse-4b on RunPod Serverless) ────────────
# The reader's "extract text" pipeline for scanned PDFs and images. The
# learner's browser rasterizes pages; each page runs one /runsync call on
# the parse worker deployed from runpod-worker/. Unset = the reader's
# extraction affordances hide (an honest 501 if called directly).
# RUNPOD_API_KEY=rpa_xxx              # RunPod API key (Settings → API Keys)
# RUNPOD_PARSE_ENDPOINT_ID=xxxxxxxxx  # the serverless endpoint running the parse worker
# PARSE_CONSOLE_KEY=choose-a-long-random-string
#                                     # arms the browser console at GET /api/parse/console?key=…
#                                     # for test-firing the parse endpoint (each run = a real GPU job)

# ── Record A/V transcription (ffmpeg → Deepgram; frames → captions) ──────────
# ── Media worker (optional, recommended) ─────────────────────────────
# The ffmpeg container (media-worker/ — Cloudflare Container or any
# Docker host). When set, BOTH heavy lanes leave this server:
#   · transcription: the ffmpeg half runs THERE; this API only pulls the
#     small artifacts (16 kHz mp3, capped frames) for Deepgram/captions
#   · course-video encoding: the upload dispatch goes straight to the
#     container (POST /jobs/encode) — media moves container ↔ R2, never
#     through this server, and no BullMQ encode queue is opened.
# The container shares this service's INTERNAL_SECRET. Unset → the
# original in-process paths run as before (ffmpeg in-process; BullMQ
# worker via `npm run worker`). With it set, the old video worker can
# stand down (VIDEO_WORKER_ENABLED=false / don't run the worker).
# MEDIA_WORKER_URL=https://akoro-media-worker.example.workers.dev

# Reuses DEEPGRAM_API_KEY (modules/voice) and FFMPEG_PATH (worker.js).
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY must be set for the lane to arm; unset = honest 501.
#
# "Always extract": uploads transcribe/parse themselves at registration —
# learner A/V uploads (POST /api/records), course lessons (lesson write +
# encode completion). The reader's manual offer remains as the retry.
# AUTO_TRANSCRIBE_UPLOADS=0 opts a deployment out of the automatic lane;
# the reader's explicit offer always works either way.
# AUTO_TRANSCRIBE_UPLOADS=1
# AV_FRAME_PROVIDER  — slide-frame captions: auto (default) uses our
#                      hanji-parse RunPod worker when extraction is
#                      configured, else gpt-4o-mini; or force
#                      hanji | openai | off.
# AV_MAX_FRAMES      — scene-frame cap per video (default 10).
# AV_SCENE_THRESHOLD — ffmpeg scene-cut sensitivity 0-1 (default 0.3).
# AV_FRAME_PROVIDER=auto
# AV_MAX_FRAMES=10
# AV_SCENE_THRESHOLD=0.3
